        "title": "build: update Turndown to 7.2.4",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- update the bundled Turndown distribution from 7.2.2 to 7.2.4\n- initialize the WebKit runtime through a bounded real navigation completion and serialize first use\n- cover upstream link/image escaping fixes and concurrent initialization\n\n## Upstream provenance\n\n- repository: https://github.com/mixmark-io/turndown\n- release comparison: https://github.com/mixmark-io/turndown/compare/v7.2.2...v7.2.4\n- package: https://www.npmjs.com/package/turndown/v/7.2.4\n- bundled payload SHA-256 after removing Demark's five-line license banner: `c97187f436d41638bf7acf346a39d9d42f2f2c02af18245a297c09e796f8e46f` (matches the official npm tarball)\n\n## Risk\n\nMedium. The generated vendor file is a large mechanical diff; the Swift runtime changes fix constructor export, concurrent first-use navigation, and unbounded blank-page waits. Initialization now stops after five seconds or WebContent process termination. Public API unchanged.\n\nFiles: 4. Diff: +328/-390.\n\n## Proof\n\n- `swift build -v`\n- `swift test -v` — 60 tests passed; live suites skipped by default\n- `DEMARK_LIVE_TESTS=1 swift test --filter DemarkURLLoading` — 26 tests passed\n- `./scripts/lint.sh`\n- `(cd Example && swift build -v)`\n- source-blind external consumer: escaping, simple conversion, and concurrent first-use contracts passed\n- deterministic initialization-timeout regression passed\n- full suite passed five consecutive times after removing a CI-load-sensitive wall-clock assertion\n- autoreview: clean after resolving the bounded-navigation finding\n- public model identifier gate: PASS\n",
